<title>MEXICO: Bancrecer says to lead new pension fund firm.</title>
<headline>Bancrecer says to lead new pension fund firm.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grupo Financiero BanCrecer, Dresdner Bank and Grupo Allianz said that they plan to form a Mexican pension fund group, known as an AFORE.</p>
<p>In a statement, they said that BanCrecer will hold a 51 percent position in the new company.</p>
<p>Several financial groups have set up AFOREs in Mexico, aiming to manage pensions when the country opens its pension system to the private sector at the start of next year.</p>
<p>&quot;The mix of local and international experience will place this AFORE in a solid position to offer quality products and services...,&quot; they said in the statement.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
</text>
